+## Filtering
+
+The list is narrowed by a name and by a set of statuses. Both are applied by the
+repository, next to the paging and the sorting, so the grid still holds one page
+at a time and the count in `Showing 15 of 500` is a count query, not a row count.
+A customer matches when every whitespace-separated term of the name filter occurs
+in its first or last name — ignoring case and accents, so `makinen` finds
+`Mäkinen` — and when its status is one of the selected ones, or none is selected.
+
+The filter is also the view's URL:
+
+```text
+/?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED
+```
+
+Opening that applies the filter and fills the two fields in; changing either
+field replaces the current history entry with the new URL, so typing does not
+fill up the back button.
